  @ ------------------------------------------------------------
  @  NormlQ
  @  Quantile: the X below which the probability is p.
  @  Author & design          : Jean Wilson
  @  Co-authors & programming  : Claude & Claude Code (Anthropic)
  @  Arguments may be given loose or bundled in a list of 3; that list is
  @  what LastArguments reports, and its length is checked before use.
  @ ------------------------------------------------------------
  IF DUP TypeName "list" == THEN IF DUP Size 3 ≠ THEN "NormlQ: needs 3 arguments" DoError END Explode Drop END
  → μv sxv pv « μv 0 + sxv 0 + pv 0 + → μ sx p « 'μ-12*sx' →Num 'μ+12*sx' →Num 0 0 → lo hi x d « 1 40 START '(lo+hi)/2' →Num 'x' STO '(0.5*(1+erf((x-μ)/(sx*√(2)))))' →Num 'd' STO 'IFTE(d<p;x;lo)' →Num 'lo' STO 'IFTE(d<p;hi;x)' →Num 'hi' STO NEXT '(lo+hi)/2' →Num 'x' STO 1 2 START 'IFTE(ABS(1/(sx*√(2*Ⓒπ))*EXP(-((x-μ)²)/(2*sx²)))>0.000000000000000000000000000001;x-((0.5*(1+erf((x-μ)/(sx*√(2)))))-p)/(1/(sx*√(2*Ⓒπ))*EXP(-((x-μ)²)/(2*sx²)));x)' →Num 'd' STO 'IFTE((d>lo) AND (d<hi);d;x)' →Num 'x' STO NEXT x μv sxv pv 3 →List Drop » » »
